/-! # PA2 (iii): the POP bank of the SYM decode, its register program

At a POP unit (a circuit row `r ≥ |carriers|`, target `s`), the decoded state holds the row `r` (`H 9`), the target
`s` (`H 12`), the cell row (`H 13`), the joint state's index `x = t mod Π` (`H 15`), the list seed's index (`H 17`),
the circuits' bottoms `m_0 … m_3` (`dM0 … dM3`), the flat list's `M, B, errExp` (`G 32 … G 34`), the carriers' counts
(`XA`, `XB`) and the circuits' total (`dMS`). The bank finds the circuit `i = (r − nc)/2` and the sign
`p = (r − nc) mod 2`, the joint state's digit `(t_i^+, t_i^−)` (`SymDecEnum.stateDigit`: divisions by `m_k + 1`), the
clamp `[s ≤ m_i]·s`, and on the clamp's match writes the POP setup's entry bank (`PopSetup.PopIn`: `ppM … ppL`) and
clears every register from `410` on.

* `sel4`; the phases `pA1W`, `pA2W` (digits and prefix sums, branch-free), `pLW` (the circuit ladder), `pTW` (the
  clamp and the match flags), `pMW` (the bank); their runs `pA1_run`, `pA2_run`, `pL_run`, `pT_run`, `pM_run`.

Paper quantities of the main types: the SYM request unit's circuit `i`, sign, joint-state digit and clamp
(`SymFlat.symReqUnit`, row:sym P3:2477-2496), and the POP row's slice (offset `2Σ|X| + Σ_{k<i} m_k`, length `m_i`). -/

